Adal is a tengu of [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], the father of [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and [[People/Galzu|Galzu]], and a noble of [[Org/Belvedere|Belvedere]]. He speaks of his family's minds as their strongest asset and looks down on art made without a patron.

He found Anzu's hiding place through the archive Anzu visited in [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]] and sent an urgent fax to the [[Sin and Tonic]] asking him to call. He had talked the rest of the family out of digging too deep, and had kept the news from Ishta, who was not happy with Anzu. He asked Anzu to call his mother now and then so the family would know he was well, and offered him another identity to use if he wanted to stay hidden.

He was more worried about Galzu, who had stormed out of the roost two days earlier and not come back. He had nothing on the break-in at the Belvedere facility itself, though the site was near where Anzu's grandmother had been that night, and he meant to put pressure on the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]] if Galzu turned out to be hiding with them.
